{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1179-i-m-creating-a-black-market-exigent-for-a-2-5-game","id":1179,"title":"I'm creating a Black Market Exigent for a 2.5 game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-02T11:29:07-07:00","id":1179,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon12.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> I'm creating a Black Market Exigent for a 2.5 game","content":"I posted this on the old forum, but I may be able to find more interested posters over here. Who knows?<br /> <br /> I'm creating a Black Market Exigent for a 2.5 game. Who wants to help? <img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/Images/Emoticons/emotion-1.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Has anyone else done this? Anyway, here's the background: A couple of years ago, I was running a solo Lunar game. The PC's antagonist, known as &quot;the nobleman,&quot; had ran and ruined the PC's life from the age of toddler to adulthood. After barely surviving the nobleman's attempt to end the PC's life, the PC exalted as a lunar. The PC dropped off the map and let the nobleman believe he was dead. He received training and tats from the Silver Pact. A few years later, the lunar sets out to free enslaved peoples, beginning with the Djalas. His plan was to establish an independent Djala nation. However, he discovered that his plans crossed the nobleman's as the nobleman had become a major slave trader of djalas. Then an event happened wherein the PC was sidelined for 100 years. Now he's back, but to his astonishment, the nobleman is still around. Unfortunately, the player had to move and our game stopped there. However, the player has recently moved back and has been interested in resuming the story.<br /> <br /> Two years ago, I wanted the nobleman to remain an effective and challenging adversary after the PC's exaltation. I wanted him to become some kind of Exalt. However, I did not want him to be a Solar, Lunar, or Sidereal. I was thinking GSP, Abyssal or even a dragonblood who had made some kind of deal with the Yozi to force a terrestrial exaltation. Maybe even make him a godblood with all the godblood abilities, so he'd be as powerful as a low level DB. But none of those seemed to jive with who the nobleman was. Fast forward two years later and the devs announce the creation of exigents and black market exaltations. This sounds like a perfect fit.<br /> <br /> The black market exigence is built around the concept of leadership of city-states. The exaltation will favor the abilities: Bureaucracy, Performance, Presence, Socialize, and War. The out-of-caste favored ability will be melee. The nobleman is a renowned fencer. I'll give him the basic abilities all current exalts share plus some anima ability that jives with the leadership vibe (if anyone has any suggestions on this, I would appreciate it). I'm thinking the DB's Ox Body, and a lunar or sidereal's essence pool. I'm not looking to reinvent the wheel; I plan on stealing liberally from the existing exalt types.<br /> <br /> The charm structure has me stumped though. I know I want it to be ability based, but other than that, I don't know. Is it going to be Ability + Attribute, or permanent Essence, or Specialty, or Virtue? A little more flavor; when the PC returns to the nobleman's city, he will find that 95% of the people are gleefully enslaved to doing the nobleman's bidding. He has used his Charms to make the people love him and strive their utmost to serve him and his needs. This kind of mind-smurfing sounds like it belongs in the Solar Charm realm, but I don't want him to be that powerful. Most of his power is going to be directed at making the city run effectively and making his serfs want to work themselves near to death to please him. The people adore and almost worship the nobleman (hm, perhaps some do). We don't really need to make the social type Charms. That will all be in the background. It's the final showdown I'm more concerned about. He will only have a few combat Charms and those will be related to swordplay.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions would be appreciated. Thanks <img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/Images/Emoticons/emotion-1.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T11:20:02-08:00","id":2790,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, creating an Exigent at this point will be exceedingly difficult, considering Exigents are based on ideas and mechanical constructs that simply don't exist in 2E.<br /> <br /> That said, it might be worth it to check out the Roll of Glorious Divinity I for their spirit Charms, as well as the Scroll of Fallen Races for some non-traditional Charm models (thanks to the Dragon Kings and Mountain Folk). It provides some ideas for how to work a non-traditional Exalt in the context of 2E. Sad to say, that's the best I can do until the actual Exigents hardback comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T16:54:06-08:00","id":5566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1179-i-m-creating-a-black-market-exigent-for-a-2-5-game?p=2790#post2790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, creating an Exigent at this point will be exceedingly difficult, considering Exigents are based on ideas and mechanical constructs that simply don't exist in 2E.<br /> <br /> That said, it might be worth it to check out the Roll of Glorious Divinity I for their spirit Charms, as well as the Scroll of Fallen Races for some non-traditional Charm models (thanks to the Dragon Kings and Mountain Folk). It provides some ideas for how to work a non-traditional Exalt in the context of 2E. Sad to say, that's the best I can do until the actual Exigents hardback comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably going to sound crazy (may even drive some crazy) but...I'm really not concerned with fleshing out the whole deal. I'm mostly interested in some low level combat charms. I'm planning on stealing liberally from other splats and either reducing the power, as in the case of Solar Charms, or increasing the power, as in the case of DB charms. I'll throw some descriptive fluff in, and my players will never realize that they are recycled Charms. Maybe add an anima ability or something. Of course what i come up with is almost guaranteed to be nowhere near what an actual Exigent will be when they finally arrive in 3E, but I figured what the heck. I love the idea of Exigents, so I'm going to use it now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:00:21-08:00","id":5572,"title":"","content":"Aaaaand, since I started this thread recently in the old Exalted forum, I'm going to copy/paste that thread into this one! <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_content text_table_postContainer_Alt\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postheader text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_postUser text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"140\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=profile&amp;u=30665\" target=\"_blank\">Suleri Drals</a> </b></td> <td class=\"text_table_postPosted text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"80%\" colspan=\"2\"> Thursday, October 31, 2013 8:23:37 PM(UTC)<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1722967#post1722967\" target=\"_blank\">#2</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_post_alt text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_UserBox text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_post_alt_td\" colspan=\"2\"> <img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/resource.ashx?u=30665\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </td> <td class=\"text_table_message text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_post_alt_td\"> Exigent is perfect for what you want.<br /> He can be relatively weak if you wish it. (so that his domination is not only magic)<br /> He can be the Chosen of a simple terrestrial god of a city-state.<br /> Or you can seek a preexistent god near. (for example, If his city has many slaves, he can be a Chosen of Rabszolga, god of slaves : he gains in power with the number of slaves in Creation.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But why the Black Market ? Black Market is for the gods who want to hide their Exigents or Forbidden Gods.<br /> Because his Patron God is probably \u201cevil\u201d ? but a very evil god can respected by the Bureaucraty. (Rabszolga is a very normal terrestial god, and slavery is actively encouraged by many people in Yu-Shan and the Terrestial Bureaucraty.)<br /> <br /> The \u201cnatural\u201d diseases as tuberculosis are as much domains managed by the gods as the chocolate, death too. (But not the Underworld, ghosts and the plague of Deathlords, of course, but as Neverborns are deads, they have largely disturbed all that is related to death.)<br /> <br /> <br /> </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postfooter text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_small text_table_postTop text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_postfooter_td\" colspan=\"3\"> | <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=messagehistory&amp;m=1722967\" target=\"_blank\">Edit by user</a><br /> </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_post_alt text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_post_alt_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_message text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_post_alt_td\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postsep text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td colspan=\"3\" class=\"text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_postsep_td\"></td> </tr> </table></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_content text_table_postContainer\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postheader text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_postUser text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"140\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=profile&amp;u=3705\" target=\"_blank\">Darkon</a> </b></td> <td class=\"text_table_postPosted text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"80%\" colspan=\"2\"> Thursday, October 31, 2013 8:47:57 PM(UTC)<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1722975#post1722975\" target=\"_blank\">#3</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_post text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_UserBox text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_post_td\" colspan=\"2\"> <img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/resource.ashx?u=3705\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </td> <td class=\"text_table_message text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_post_td\"> Good questions. It's possible I may not know or understand all that has been revealed so far regarding Exigents or Black Market Exaltations. When the devs mentioned BMEs, I imagined shadowy groups capturing gods and rendering them against their will into exaltations. Then, the exaltation is passed around among various powers for tweaking until they get what they want out of it. That's how I imagined the nobleman getting his power; illegitimately.<br /> <br /> </td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:01:17-08:00","id":5575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_content text_table_postContainer_Alt\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postheader text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_postUser text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"140\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=profile&amp;u=30665\" target=\"_blank\">Suleri Drals</a> </b></td> <td class=\"text_table_postPosted text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"80%\" colspan=\"2\"> Thursday, October 31, 2013 8:23:37 PM(UTC)<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1722967#post1722967\" target=\"_blank\">#2</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_post_alt text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_UserBox text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_post_alt_td\" colspan=\"2\"> <img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/resource.ashx?u=30665\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </td> <td class=\"text_table_message text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_post_alt_td\"> Exigent is perfect for what you want.<br /> He can be relatively weak if you wish it. (so that his domination is not only magic)<br /> He can be the Chosen of a simple terrestrial god of a city-state.<br /> Or you can seek a preexistent god near. (for example, If his city has many slaves, he can be a Chosen of Rabszolga, god of slaves : he gains in power with the number of slaves in Creation.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But why the Black Market ? Black Market is for the gods who want to hide their Exigents or Forbidden Gods.<br /> Because his Patron God is probably \u201cevil\u201d ? but a very evil god can respected by the Bureaucraty. (Rabszolga is a very normal terrestial god, and slavery is actively encouraged by many people in Yu-Shan and the Terrestial Bureaucraty.)<br /> <br /> The \u201cnatural\u201d diseases as tuberculosis are as much domains managed by the gods as the chocolate, death too. (But not the Underworld, ghosts and the plague of Deathlords, of course, but as Neverborns are deads, they have largely disturbed all that is related to death.)<br /> <br /> <br /> </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postfooter text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"></tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:03:17-08:00","id":5576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_content text_table_postContainer\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postheader text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_postUser text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"140\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=profile&amp;u=3705\" target=\"_blank\">Darkon</a> </b></td> <td class=\"text_table_postPosted text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"80%\" colspan=\"2\"> Thursday, October 31, 2013 8:47:57 PM(UTC)<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1722975#post1722975\" target=\"_blank\">#3</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_post text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_UserBox text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_post_td\" colspan=\"2\"> <img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/resource.ashx?u=3705\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </td> <td class=\"text_table_message text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_post_td\"> Good questions. It's possible I may not know or understand all that has been revealed so far regarding Exigents or Black Market Exaltations. When the devs mentioned BMEs, I imagined shadowy groups capturing gods and rendering them against their will into exaltations. Then, the exaltation is passed around among various powers for tweaking until they get what they want out of it. That's how I imagined the nobleman getting his power; illegitimately.<br /> <br /> </td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:04:49-08:00","id":5578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_content text_table_postContainer_Alt\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postheader text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_postUser text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"140\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=profile&amp;u=30665\" target=\"_blank\">Suleri Drals</a> </b></td> <td class=\"text_table_postPosted text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"80%\" colspan=\"2\"> Thursday, October 31, 2013 8:53:18 PM(UTC)<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1722976#post1722976\" target=\"_blank\">#4</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_post_alt text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_UserBox text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_post_alt_td\" colspan=\"2\"> <img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/resource.ashx?u=30665\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </td> <td class=\"text_table_message text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_post_alt_td\"> Hrmmm...<br /> <br /> Don't you confuse with \u201cDirty Bomb Exalts\u201d? the Black Market resells exigences but created by only one god.<br /> <br /> To mix the Essence is very dangerous and create Exigents unstable but powerful. (Dirty Bomb)<br /> <br /> Yes his exigence could have been bought in Black Market.<br /> the Guild is the only organization mortal with being able to do that, I think?<br /> <br /> </td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:06:00-08:00","id":5579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_wysiwyg_table_content text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_postheader text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_tr text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_postUser text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postheader_td\" width=\"140\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=profile&amp;u=22716\" target=\"_blank\">Gaius</a> </b></td> <td class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_postPosted text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postheader_td\" width=\"80%\" colspan=\"2\">Thursday, October 31, 2013 9:44:47 PM(UTC)<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1723000#post1723000\" target=\"_blank\">#5</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_post text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_tr text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_UserBox text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_post_td\" colspan=\"2\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_message text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_post_td\"><b>Gaius wrote:</b> Suleri is mostly in the right. As I understand it, creating an Exigent to create an Exigent is normally accomplished by a god requesting and receiving permission from the Unconquered Sun to access the Divine Exigence. A Black Market Exaltation is when that access is granted, but sold or stolen, such that it is ultimately used by a deity who may not be in the Unconquered Sun's good graces.<br /> <br /> Here's John himself on Black Market Exaltations and &quot;dirty bomb&quot; Exalts:<br /> <br /> <b>John M\u00f8rke wrote:</b> As some people have begun to speculate, the Black Market Exaltations refer to Exigents made illicitly, somehow bypassing the Unconquered Sun's erm firewall, so to speak.<br /> <br /> In the most literal terms, there were raw Exaltations granted by the Unconquered Sun which were then not used by the petitioner, but instead passed into the world of spirits, where it cycled the realms of gods and men until a bidder was finally able to trigger it.<br /> <br /> A &quot;dirty bomb&quot; (not actual game term) Exaltation is a similar concept, only the Exaltation has passed through the hands of multiple spirits who have modified the power inside. This only happens for nefarious, terrible reasons, as the resulting Exigent is always an aberration of enormous power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gaius wrote:</b> Legitimately acquired or not, creating an Exigent still involves some non-trivial sacrifice on the part of the god. Perhaps &quot;dirty bombs&quot; require lesser sacrifice, shouldered by several deities as it is?<br /> <br /> I doubt The Guild is alone in being able to buy them, but doing so would certainly demand throwing around a ton of moolah to make it worth it to a deity to brave the risks. A god with access to creating an Exigent at all isn't the sort of thing one finds everyday. Your mortal nobleman even without deep pockets could conceivably get such a god to Choose him: he'd just need to find the right price.<br /> <br /> Or, possibly, convince the deity the price is much lower than it actually is. Perhaps he's persuasive enough to get a god to believe that he has come into possession of a wondrous object of great power. This potent tool &quot;supplements&quot; the process, ensuring even a weak deity can survive the ordeal with minimal loss. Naturally, he will only use this great gift to carry out the god's will in ways only the Exalted can. Said deity is completely fleeced and goes for it. The nobleman thus becomes an Exigent by tricking a god into obliterating itself. Illegitimate enough for ya? <img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/Images/Emoticons/emotion-5.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Bonus points if the god gained Exigency access in the proper fashion and was legitimately trying to do right by its worshipers when he was conned -- perhaps the god really was revered and loved, such that becoming said god's Chosen (and keeping the true story under wraps) gave the nobleman a population that adored him he was happy to exploit. Not all impressive feats need to be achieved through Charms, after all, though such adoration would probably grease the wheels on whatever Social Charms he has.</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":362,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","user":"Darkon","date":".  Legibility 11-07-2013, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:07:15-08:00","id":5583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_wysiwyg_table_content text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_Alt\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_postheader text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_tr text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_postUser text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postheader_td\" width=\"140\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=profile&amp;u=6702\" target=\"_blank\">Limited Reagent</a> </b></td> <td class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_postPosted text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postheader_td\" width=\"80%\" colspan=\"2\">Thursday, October 31, 2013 10:00:58 PM(UTC)<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1723006#post1723006\" target=\"_blank\">#6</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_post_alt text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_tr text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_UserBox text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_post_alt_td\" colspan=\"2\"><img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/resource.ashx?u=6702\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></td> <td class=\"text_table_wysiwyg_table_message text_table_wysiwyg_table_content_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_wysiwyg_table_post_alt_td\"><b>Darkon wrote:</b> The charm structure has me stumped though. I know I want it to be ability based, but other than that, I don't know. Is it going to be Ability + Attribute, or permanent Essence, or Specialty, or Virtue? A little more flavor; when the PC returns to the nobleman's city, he will find that 95% of the people are gleefully enslaved to doing the nobleman's bidding. He has used his Charms to make the people love him and strive their utmost to serve him and his needs. This kind of mind-smurfing sounds like it belongs in the Solar Charm realm, but I don't want him to be that powerful. Most of his power is going to be directed at making the city run effectively and making his serfs want to work themselves near to death to please him. The people adore and almost worship the nobleman (hm, perhaps some do). We don't really need to make the social type Charms. That will all be in the background. It's the final showdown I'm more concerned about. He will only have a few combat Charms and those will be related to swordplay.<br /> <br /> <b>Limited Reagent wrote:</b> If you want to go weird, have his dice cap based on the Magnitude of whatever group he leads, up to a max of 10. This also gives the PCs something interesting to do if they find out about this: if they start removing people from his group (by whatever means) they weaken him personally.<br /> <br /> A good way to do Charms, if you want simple, is to take a Solar Charm and cut it down in scope. Like take Husband-Seducing Demon Dance and cut it down to just being loyalty to the city-state. But as you said, you want this to be background stuff.<br /> <br /> For combat, it might be worth looking to Sidereals, if you don't want just melee Charms. They have some interesting social combat stuff like You and Yours Stance that could pretty easily be refluffed to work. As far as those swordplay Charms, think about making them work only within the laws of the city-state. I mean, like say the city-state has a dueling culture. His Charms, then, only work (or work to their full potential) when he's officially initiated a duel. He might also have Charms that allow him to shunt damage or attacks over to underlings, either supernaturally (the man is stabbed but it does nothing; his servant collapses in blood) or they just reflexively leap in front of the attack and take the blow. Sort of like granting underlings limited use of Virtuous Negation Defense from the DBs. Something similar to Throne Shadow Charms would probably work well too, though likely more overt so they're based around swordplay and command rather than martial arts and power behind the throne.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Another interesting twist you might want to consider is if this Exaltation is a one-time deal, or if it has any type of reincarnation built into it. Ie if/when this guy is defeated/killed, who if anyone will the power go to next? It could go to the next ruler of the city-state, maybe, or this guy's heir. Maybe there is some symbol of office that, whoever holds it next Exalts. There are a lot of ways you could do it. Make some shit up that you think will be fun.\u2122<br /> \u2014<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> </td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":362,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","user":"Darkon","date":".  Legibility 11-07-2013, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:08:03-08:00","id":5584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_content text_table_postContainer\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postheader text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_postUser text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"140\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=profile&amp;u=22716\" target=\"_blank\">Gaius</a> </b></td> <td class=\"text_table_postPosted text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"80%\" colspan=\"2\"> Thursday, October 31, 2013 10:31:11 PM(UTC)<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1723015#post1723015\" target=\"_blank\">#7</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_post text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_UserBox text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_post_td\" colspan=\"2\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_message text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_post_td\"> Ooh, really good ideas in there, Reagent. ^__^ For Charm concepts, it may also be worth pilfering ideas from Theion's Charmset in Shards of the Exalted Dream. Though it's been some time since I read it, I admit. May be worth scaling back the power level and/or toning down the divine imagery, but I remember the basic idea of leadership and power dependent on one's underlings being very big in there.<br /> <br /> I also agree with the possibility of continuity for the Exaltation. Depending on whether the nobleman is actually the first to carry it, this could run both ways, though 'what comes after' feels far more interesting. Would the new recipient turn out to be of a similar mold to the nobleman? Someone far more amenable to the Lunar? Or someone who <i>might</i> be more amenable, had the nobleman's memories not left enough of an impression to color the new heir's view of the Lunar.<br /> <br /> </td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:08:40-08:00","id":5585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_content text_table_postContainer_Alt\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postheader text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_postUser text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"140\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=profile&amp;u=6187\" target=\"_blank\">hobbitguy1420</a> </b></td> <td class=\"text_table_postPosted text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_postheader_td\" width=\"80%\" colspan=\"2\"> Friday, November 01, 2013 3:16:08 PM(UTC)<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1723304#post1723304\" target=\"_blank\">#8</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_post_alt text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_Alt_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_UserBox text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_post_alt_td\" colspan=\"2\"> <img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/resource.ashx?u=6187\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </td> <td class=\"text_table_message text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_Alt_td text_table_post_alt_td\"> This is for an NPC, right? Not a full-on player character?<br /> <br /> That makes it easier, as you don't have to work out a bunch of the &quot;make this kosher for PCs&quot; stuff for his powers - they can be more like a panoply power in one of the NPC spirit writeups. Prerequisites don't really matter - either he has the power or he doesn't.<br /> <br /> As for thematics, I'd figure out how esoteric you want to go - is he a straightforward &quot;control the city&quot; sort, with relatively logical ties, or is he a more philosophical sort like the Sidereals, interpreting cityhood though the lens of something else and vice versa in his powerset?<br /> <br /> Specific power ideas:<br /> Look at the world through the windows of his city's buildings (Awareness)<br /> Mystically mess with traffic in his city, increasing/decreasing the travel times for his foes or allies (bureaucracy or something)<br /> Make the walls and streets of his city resound with his words, transmitting social attacks (Performance)<br /> Reshape the city itself, leaving unwanted visitors hopelessly lost (Crafts or Survival)<br /> Wrap himself in armor (or transform himself into a creature) of brick and stone, making the walls of the city his bones and the cobblestones his skin. (Resistance or Crafts)<br /> Subsume his consciousness entirely into the city, letting him control the things within while leaving his body comatose.<br /> Transfer knowledge among those in his thrall, so that if one member has a given skill at 4, *everyone* has that skill at 4, while motes are committed.<br /> Destroy part of the city to heal himself, or sacrifice those under his thrall for the same.<br /> <br /> Maybe use a dice cap of (Ability + Level of the Followers background)?<br /> <br /> </td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:19:17-08:00","id":5595,"title":"","content":"<b>&quot;Darkon&quot; wrote: </b>It seems I did not fully understand all that has been revealed regarding Black Market Exaltations (BME). I thought all BMEs were &quot;dirty bomb&quot; exaltations, but apparently that's not the case. Thanks everyone so far, there's been a lot of good suggestions. That's awesome. <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Gaius&quot; wrote:</b> Perhaps &quot;dirty bombs&quot; require lesser sacrifice, shouldered by several deities as it is?<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Darkon&quot; wrote: </b>That's exactly what I was thinking. More specifically, there are a ton of jobless/technically homeless gods in Yu Shan as a result of Creation shrinking after the Balorian Crusade. I could see a group of gods, working together in Yu Shan and Creation to form this BME ring. They begin the process by godnapping one of these jobless/homeless deities (who won't be missed) and then torture them until they impress their power onto a exigent shard. The Law of Diminshment kicks in and destroys the deity. This exigent shard would then either be passed to a buyer or pass through a series of deities as they tweak it and power it up before passing it along to a buyer. I'm thinking that if a group of deities work together, they can pool their power to tweak these illicit exigent shards without running afoul of the Law of Diminishment. <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Limited Reagent&quot; wrote:</b> A good way to do Charms, if you want simple, is to take a Solar Charm and cut it down in scope. Like take Husband-Seducing Demon Dance and cut it down to just being loyalty to the city-state. But as you said, you want this to be background stuff. For combat, it might be worth looking to Sidereals, if you don't want just melee Charms. They have some interesting social combat stuff like You and Yours Stance that could pretty easily be refluffed to work.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Darkon&quot; wrote: </b>I like this. I think this may work for me. Others have posted some really interesting and flavorful bases for Charms, but toning down or tweaking existing Charms. <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Limited Reagent&quot; wrote:</b> Another interesting twist you might want to consider is if this Exaltation is a one-time deal, or if it has any type of reincarnation built into it.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Darkon&quot; wrote: </b>I think I'm going to go with a one-time deal. The exigent shard is permanently fused to his lower soul. So, when the PC eventually defeats him and sends him to the Underworld, the ramped-up lower soul could still be a menace. That's what I love about Exalted. Sometimes death doesn't mean the antagonist is through screwing with you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Gaius&quot; wrote:</b> For Charm concepts, it may also be worth pilfering ideas from Theion's Charmset in Shards of the Exalted Dream. Though it's been some time since I read it, I admit.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Darkon&quot; wrote: </b>Good suggestion. It's been a while since I read those as well. I'll have to give them another look. <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;hobbitguy1420&quot; wrote:</b> This is for an NPC, right? Not a full-on player character?<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Darkon&quot; wrote: </b>Correct. I'm not that ambitious. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}